<h1>Katherine S. Dunneback</h1>
<p>Chicago Board of Education, District 9b, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Endorsed by the Chicago Teachers Union.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Dunneback has said she is running as a progressive candidate focused on student services, particularly ensuring that services for students with IEPs are fully funded. She has also pointed to overcrowding at local schools, saying high-performing but under-resourced schools need long-term solutions rather than temporary annexes that become permanent.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Speech-language pathologist with 22 years of experience in public and private school settings, currently an adjunct clinical supervisor at St. Xavier University; she is a CPS parent of two former Clissold Elementary students.</p>
